<%
# ggen_igniter EEx template -> lib/beam4pm_pro_ocpm_discovery.ex
#
# beam4pm_pro gap-closure item PRO-011 ("object-centric process mining
# discovery slice") -- flagship differentiator per the deep-research
# synthesis of 2026-08-31 (verified 3-0/2-0 against Celonis Process Sphere /
# Apromore OCPM / academic OCPM literature: convergence/divergence problems
# that single-case-notion event logs cannot express).
#
# Deliberately scoped to what beam4pm's existing OCEL record types
# (ocel_event, ocel_object) can support today WITHOUT inventing new
# ontology facts: per-object-type interaction counting (how many distinct
# object types co-occur on the same event) and object-type activity
# frequency -- the two OCPM primitives every downstream algorithm (object
# graphs, divergence/convergence detection, multi-instance DFGs) is built
# on. NOT a full academic OCPM discovery algorithm (no object-centric
# Petri net synthesis, no divergence-free event log transformation) --
# that is future work this module's evidence.gaps field names honestly
# rather than silently omitting.
